<title>BELGIUM: MeesPierson's Kuiper appointed to ASLK-CGER board.</title>
<headline>MeesPierson's Kuiper appointed to ASLK-CGER board.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian bank  ASLK-CGER said on Tuesday Dutch MeesPierson chairman Joos Kuiper had been appointed to its board.</p>
<p>ASLK-CGER is controlled by Belgo-Dutch banking and insurance group  Fortis, which acquired MeesPierson last year.</p>
<p>Fortis is owned jointly by Fortis AG and Fortis AMEV.</p>
<p>ASLK-CGER said Wilfried Van Dooren, vice-chairman of bank SNCI/NMKN, another Fortis unit, had also been appointed.</p>
<p>Fortis is presently in talks with the Belgian government about lifting its 49.9 percent stake in ASLK-CGER.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
